# tools/r/readme_reach_witness.rish -- from the front door, every living door opens.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/r/readme_reach_witness.rish
#
# WHY. Four guards already read links and each asks a different question: `tracked_link` about
# symlinks landing inside the tracked tree, `seed_link` about surviving the public projection,
# `foundations_link` about one room, `living_docs_lint` as a tree-wide advisory nobody gates on.
# None asked the newcomer's question -- start at README.md, follow links, does every door open?
#
# Measured the first time on `20260823`: 1,389 documents reached fifteen levels deep, and 1,209
# broken links. **1,097 of those stood in dated testimony**, which the mark law resolves rather than
# rewrites, and **112 stood in 42 living files**, where a broken link is simply broken. The 112 are
# repaired -- 97 by suffix-unique repoint, 205 index rows given their day-folded prefix, 87 rows
# whose logs never landed in any commit delinked and marked, and 15 by hand -- and this holds the
# living count at zero.
#
# WHAT IS GATED, hard, at zero. Broken relative links in LIVING files reachable from README.md,
# where living means the basename carries no one-clock stamp -- the same rule the dated-path
# repointer applies, so the two can never disagree about what testimony is.
#
# WHAT IS REPORTED, and deliberately NOT ratcheted. Broken links in dated testimony. A ceiling was
# tried here and removed on the lap it was written: adding ONE index page reached five more documents
# and the testimony count rose with them, so the ratchet punished the tree for opening a door. The
# LOST-reference duty is already owned with no slack by `tools/d/dated_path_witness.rish`, and a
# second meter over one quantity is how two meters come to disagree. Testimony is resolved rather
# than rewritten: `rishi/bin/rishi run tools/d/dated_path_resolve.rish <reference>`.
#
# Pen: tools/fixtures/readme_reach_control.sh -- eight cases, a living break bitten and named, the
# same break in testimony counted rather than gated, the ceiling proven to bite, an unreached
# document out of scope, and an http target never followed. Run from the repository root.

say "readme-reach: Language EN -- a newcomer follows links, and a door that fails to open is the tree's word breaking."
say "readme-reach: Style Gauge -- the count is split by tier, because testimony is resolved and living prose is repaired."
say "readme-reach: Lens TAME -- safety first: a link is a promise, and this rung is where the promise is checked."

let scan = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/readme_reach_scan.sh"]
say scan.out
assert scan.ok else "readme-reach: a living document reachable from the front door holds a broken link -- read the scan's own lines"
assert scan.out contains "verdict=ok" else "readme-reach: the crawl must reach a clean verdict"
assert scan.out contains "broken_in_living=0" else "readme-reach: living prose must hold no broken link"
assert scan.out contains "living_files_affected=0" else "readme-reach: no living file may carry one"

let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/readme_reach_control.sh"]
assert control.ok else "readme-reach: the control must complete"
say control.out
assert control.out contains "case=clean_free ok" else "readme-reach: a tree whose links resolve must pass"
assert control.out contains "case=depth_walked ok" else "readme-reach: the crawl must follow links past one level"
assert control.out contains "case=living_bitten ok" else "readme-reach: a broken link in a living file must be refused"
assert control.out contains "case=living_named ok" else "readme-reach: the refusal must name the file and the target"
assert control.out contains "case=testimony_ratchets ok" else "readme-reach: the same break in dated testimony is counted, never gated"
assert control.out contains "case=testimony_never_gates ok" else "readme-reach: testimony must be reported and never refused -- the LOST duty belongs to dated_path_witness"
assert control.out contains "case=unreached_free ok" else "readme-reach: a document the front door never reaches is out of scope"
assert control.out contains "case=external_free ok" else "readme-reach: an http target is never followed and never counted"
assert control.out contains "control=ok" else "readme-reach: the control must agree with itself"

say "RED and GREEN paths proven -- a living break bitten and named, testimony reported and never gated"
say "GREEN: readme-reach -- from the front door, every living door opens."
